#: content/for/activists.md:40
msgid "Developed by humans, for humans"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:42
msgid ""
"KDE e.V. is a German non-profit foundation, and our software is primarily "
"developed by volunteers from all over the world. Unlike our competitors, we "
"don't seek to make money, but instead seek to make the world a better place. "
"We envision a world where monopolistic corporations and repressive "
"governments don't have too much power over our digital lives. We actually "
"care about data privacy and digital well-being, and we fight for them."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:53
msgid ""
"<div class=\"row\">\n"
"  <div class=\"col-12 col-lg-6\">\n"
"    <h2 class=\"mt-0\">KDE Eco</h2>\n"
"    <p class=\"text-left\">KDE supports the FEEP and BE4FOSS programs to "
"help free and open-source communities produce more environmentally friendly "
"software. The projects provide communities with guidelines and support to "
"optimize software to be more energy efficient and have a longer life-span.</"
"p>\n"
"    <a href=\"https://eco.kde.org/\" class=\"btn btn-outline-light btn-lg mx-"
"auto\">Learn more</a>\n"
"    <h3>Okular Awarded Blue Angel Ecolabel</h3>\n"
"    <p>In 2022, KDE's popular multi-platform PDF reader and universal "
"document viewer Okular became the first ever Blue Angel eco-certified "
"computer program! Blue Angel is the German version of the U.S. Energy Star "
"label.</p>\n"
"    <a href=\"https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-03-16-press-release-okular-blue-"
"angel/\" class=\"btn btn-outline-light btn-lg mx-auto\" alt=\"\">Learn more</"
"a>\n"
"  </div>\n"
"  <div class=\"col-12 col-lg-6\">\n"
"    <img src=\"okular.png\" class=\"img-fluid kirigami-devices\" alt=\"\" /"
">\n"
"  </div>\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:71
msgid "End to End Encryption"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:73
msgid ""
"Everyone has a right to privacy, but for activists, ensuring the privacy and "
"security of communication can become a matter of life and death."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:77
msgid "Keep your emails private with KMail"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:79
msgid ""
"KDE's email client KMail provides world-class GnuPG integration, which makes "
"it easy to encrypt your emails. GnuPG is a global standard which was for "
"example used by [Edward Snowden to communicate with journalists](https://"
"theintercept.com/2014/10/28/smuggling-snowden-secrets/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:83
msgid "![](kmail.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:85
msgid ""
"KDE also offers [Kleopatra](https://apps.kde.org/kleopatra/), an "
"approachable app to manage multiple cryptographic certificates."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:90
msgid "Keep your messages private with NeoChat"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:92
msgid ""
"For real-time end-to-end encrypted communication, KDE has developed NeoChat, "
"a client for the [decentralized and secure messaging protocol: Matrix]"
"(https://matrix.org). It's secure and contains many features that make "
"talking with your community a breeze, including support for multiple "
"accounts, stickers, emoji reactions, and more."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:98
msgid "![](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/neochat/application.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:100
msgid ""
"The application is available on [Linux](https://flathub.org/apps/org.kde."
"neochat) and [Windows](https://apps.microsoft.com/store/detail/"
"neochat/9PNXWVNRC29H)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:104
msgid "Keep your files private with Plasma Vault"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:106
msgid ""
"Plasma Vault lets you add another layer of security by storing files and "
"folders in a super-secure encrypted container. Plasma Vault can optionally "
"disable WiFi and Bluetooth when unlocked, providing extra protection on an "
"untrusted network."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:110
msgid ""
"Plasma Vault can also be used on top of [full disk encryption](https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Disk_encryption) for even more security."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:113
msgid "![](plasma-vault.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:119
msgid "Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:121
msgid ""
"Privacy is one of our core values at KDE. We don't track you, we don't "
"collect any data about you or your behavior, we don't show you personalized "
"ads (or ads at all), we don't throw cookies at you, and we don't sell any "
"data to third parties."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:125
msgid ""
"As a general rule, software produced by the KDE Community does not transmit "
"or otherwise transfer information from end-users devices except as a result "
"of an explicit user action. Examples of this would include visiting "
"webpages, sending emails, and downloading new content (such as desktop "
"wallpapers)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:130
msgid ""
"Some pieces of KDE software may include telemetry components, which provide "
"details to KDE about the device it's running on. Where this functionality "
"exists, it is always operated on an opt-in basis and disabled by default, "
"with the ability to change your preferences at any time and inspect the data "
"it sends."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:141 content/for/travelers.md:67
msgid "Local first"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:143
msgid ""
"Synchronize your devices with [KDE Connect](https://kdeconnect.kde.org/) "
"using your local network instead of storing your data on the cloud, which "
"consumes a lot of energy and exposes your private data to the cloud provider."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:149
msgid ""
"Alternatively, check out [Nextcloud](https://nextcloud.com/) which lets you "
"create your own cloud on a private personal server, ensuring that your data "
"never leaves your custody. Many pieces of KDE software integrate with "
"NextCloud."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:158
msgid "Spread the word with Tokodon"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:160
msgid ""
"Tokodon is a client for [Mastodon](https://joinmastodon.org/), a social "
"network that is not for sale and not controlled by mercurial billionaires "
"with over-inflated egos."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:168
msgid "![](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/tokodon/tokodon-desktop.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:170
msgid ""
"Tokodon supports most of Mastodon's features, as well as multiple accounts "
"so you can manage your group and personal lives in one app."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/activists.md:173
msgid ""
"Tokodon is also compatible with other fediverse servers like [Pixelfed]"
"(https://pixelfed.org/), [GoToSocial](https://gotosocial.org/), [Akkoma]"
"(https://akkoma.dev/AkkomaGang/akkoma/) and more."
msgstr ""

