#: content/for/travelers.md:47
msgid "KDE Itinerary"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:49
msgid ""
"KDE Itinerary is a digital travel assistant that protects your privacy. It "
"makes collecting all the information about your travel inside a single "
"application easy and straightforward. KDE Itinerary is available for [Plasma "
"Mobile](https://plasma-mobile.org/) and Android."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:57
msgid "Store your reservations"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:59
msgid ""
"Store all the information about your reservations in Itinerary. This "
"includes QR-codes, check-in times, arrivial times, real-time delays, seat "
"reservations, coach layout, and more."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:61
msgid ""
"Itinerary supports train, bus and flight bookings, as well as hotel, "
"restaurant, event and rental car reservations. Traveling in a group? Not a "
"problem, Itinerary supports multi-traveler bookings."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:69
msgid ""
"Itinerary automatically extracts booking data from various input formats. "
"It's all performed locally on **your** device and your data is not sent to "
"any remote servers."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:71
msgid ""
"This works best when using [KMail](https://kontact.kde.org/components/"
"kmail/) to extract tickets from your email and then [KDE Connect](https://"
"kdeconnect.kde.org) to transfer tickets to your phone. This also works great "
"with [Nextcloud Mail](https://apps.nextcloud.com/apps/mail) and [DavDroid]"
"(https://f-droid.org/en/packages/at.bitfire.davdroid/) to sync your tickets "
"from [Nextcloud](https://nextcloud.com/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:73
msgid ""
"![KMail ticket extraction showing a train trip from Berlin to Tübingen]"
"(kmail.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:79
msgid "Add your connections"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:81
msgid ""
"Aside from finding reservations automatically in your email, Itinerary lets "
"you add train trips manually to your journey, find alternative connections "
"if your train is cancelled, or, for some providers, import your train trip "
"directly from your reservation number."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:87
msgid "Find your way"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:89
msgid ""
"Powered by [OpenStreetMap](https://www.openstreetmap.org), the indoor map at "
"train stations or airports can be a life saver. Use Itinerary to locate your "
"platform is, and, if you have seat reservation and the train layout is "
"available, it can even show you exactly which platform section is best for "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:91
msgid ""
"![Train station map in KDE Itinerary, highlighting relevant platform "
"sections.](https://www.volkerkrause.eu/assets/posts/139/kde-itinerary-"
"platform-section-highlighting.jpg)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:93
msgid ""
"The indoor map also shows you which shops and resturantes are currently "
"open, which elevator is broken (yet again!), where the toilets are and where "
"the correct exit is."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:99
msgid "Real time"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:101
msgid ""
"It is rare that a train or bus departs or arrives on time. Itinerary keeps "
"you updated when delays are announced."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:103
msgid ""
"On supported train and long distance buses, Itinerary will also use the "
"onboard APIs to fetch the current live status of the vehicle and keep you "
"updated on your current position and any announcements."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:109
msgid "Arianna"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:111
msgid ""
"Arianna is an excellent ebook reader that lets you read your favorite books "
"while traveling. Arianna will track your reading progress and classify your "
"books by genre and author automatically."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:116
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Arianna](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/arianna/reader.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:122
msgid "Kasts"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:124
msgid ""
"Enjoy listening to podcasts on the move with Kasts! Subscribe to your "
"favorite podcasts and get updated as soon as a new episode is out."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:128
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Kasts](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/kasts/kasts-desktop."
"png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:130
msgid ""
"Kasts is also available on Android and [Plasma Mobile](https://plasma-mobile."
"org)."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:142
msgid "KGeoTag"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:144
msgid ""
"KGeoTag is a geotagging program. It lets you tag your images with "
"geocoordinates by matching them to a corresponding GPX track or by manually "
"setting them by drag and dropping the images, or entering the coordinates by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:146
msgid ""
"It is very helpful in combination with [KPhotoAlbum](https://www.kphotoalbum."
"org/) or [Digikam](https://www.digikam.org/) when you want to organize your "
"photo collection after your trip and then visualize all the locations you "
"visited."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:150
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of KGeoTag showing a track on a map with some image preview "
"allong the track](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/kgeotag/kgeotag_shadow.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:156
msgid "Marble"
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:158
msgid ""
"Explore the world with Marble. Marble contains a huge collection of maps "
"that let you travel all over the globe from your desktop. Visit remote "
"places via detailed satellite images, travel the world before the discovery "
"of America, and check out the average temperature and precipitation in "
"winter and summer in other countries."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:160
msgid ""
"Marble also allows you to bookmark your favorite locations and lets you find "
"your way thanks to its routing algorithm and OpenStreetMap powered maps."
msgstr ""

#: content/for/travelers.md:164
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Kasts](https://cdn.kde.org/screenshots/marble/marble-world."
"png)"
msgstr ""

